WEBVTT

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.390
This wind is so strong!

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:08.300
What did we go to the public bath for again?!

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.980
I just hope you don't blow away, Chief.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:12.270
Don't worry about it.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:15.160
People don't just blow away that easily.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.880
Mika-chan?

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:23.320
Mika-chan, are you all right?

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:27.890
I can totally drink to them helping each other out.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:31.390
Kana, do something!

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:33.130
Well, what do you want me to do?

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:35.200
Couldn't she just let go of the umbrella?

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.340
You're right!

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.770
Kana!

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:47.600
Grandma, help!

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:51.570
Ouch...

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:54.260
Excuse me!

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:55.800
Huh?

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:56.870
Kana...

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:58.420
Long time no see.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.990
What are you two doing out on a day like this?

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:06.700
Well, it's Miss Hosomaki's birthday tomorrow,

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:08.900
our cooking club teacher.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:10.190
So we were thinking that we'd...

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:10.710
Huh?

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:15.790
Well, it's just that you've gotten so busy

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:17.950
since your grandma died.

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:20.310
I guess we forgot to tell you.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:22.720
Oh, I see.

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:33.990
Grandma, everyone is very nice and kind.

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:37.930
But it must be the typhoon's fault

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:41.410
that my heart feels all weird.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:24.850
My First Scary Story

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:27.560
Hey, Kana-chan!

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:28.800
Yes?

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:31.470
You used to be in the cooking club, right?

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:32.670
Yeah.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:35.190
The school paid for the ingredients you used,

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:39.090
which meant that you got a free dinner once a week.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:39.780
Ah.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:43.410
Well, was there anything special you did

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:46.260
for the teacher's birthday?

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:51.130
It was sort of a club tradition for all of us

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:56.630
to make a cake for the teacher's birthday.

00:03:57.150 --> 00:04:00.850
I helped too last year, but it looks like they

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:04.390
didn't want to disturb me this year.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:07.990
I guess it's because of everything that happened with my Grandma.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:14.360
So that means you're going to bake a cake for me this year!

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:17.490
I'll make a cake too!

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:22.230
Yume's cake... Yume's cake... Yume's cake...

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:25.320
Like I care. Like I give a fig!

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:29.580
We have to make sure to shut the shutters

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.740
before we go to bed tonight.

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:33.300
Yeah.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:34.940
This kind of wind and rain

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:37.310
could really wreak some havoc on this house.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:42.050
Then we'll close the shutters on the second floor!

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:43.300
Yume's cake... Yume's...

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:45.170
Let's go, Yuuki.

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:47.570
I'm going to help you too!

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:50.800
Help! She's touching my butt!

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:54.080
Then Mika and I will close up the first floor.

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:57.920
Why do I have to help the Fuushin close up?

00:04:57.920 --> 00:04:59.700
So, are you saying

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:03.160
you're going to walk home all alone in this wind and rain?

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:04.550
Sure! I'll be fine.

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:06.790
This typhoon isn't that bad.

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:12.360
Oh look, a soaked little princess!

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:15.680
She needs my help!

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:20.550
Help me already!

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:21.720
Typhoons are scary.

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:23.390
She's not dead yet.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:28.940
Do it properly!

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:35.690
Damn, I'm soaked.

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:40.180
Dripping

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:40.200
Well, if you're already soaked, you might as well be dripping.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.210
You've got to be kidding me.

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:46.420
Noo Hinata, you have to learn from Kana-chan and Mika-chan.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:49.590
Look at their wet, see-through outfits!

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:58.330
I'll get a towel.

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:01.230
I'm coming too.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:10.920
Really, everybody here is really high-strung.

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:12.420
I guess so.

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:17.280
When someone says one thing, another person rebuts it.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:20.440
Does nobody get along here?

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:24.480
I wouldn't say they're not getting along;

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:26.950
it's actually the opposite.

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:38.720
I'm scared! Grandma, I'm scared! Help me Grandma!

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:37.190
Kana, are you okay?

00:06:37.190 --> 00:06:38.690
I dropped my glasses!

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:42.180
Everyone, calm down! It's just a blackout.

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:45.590
Someone, bring a light!

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:56.820
Sorry, we were using this up on the second floor.

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:58.650
For what, exactly?

00:06:58.650 --> 00:06:59.900
Well...

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:06.560
Oh, that was so scary.

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:09.600
I just can't stand the dark.

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:11.560
Viva la blackout!

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:15.630
That's right! The show's about to start!

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:19.500
It was just a joke...

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:23.460
This is all your fault, Kana!

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:25.890
You got all freaked out.

00:07:25.890 --> 00:07:28.840
I can't help it; I get so scared in the dark!

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:45.540
These should last us until morning.

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:47.750
I'm glad you had these.

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:51.840
But I'm surprised you lit so many at once.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:54.610
It just happened, okay?

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:59.320
Oh, did you light these for me?

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:04.640
No. This building we live in is very old.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:08.230
If you let out another scream like that,

00:08:08.230 --> 00:08:09.840
the entire neighborhood would be saying...

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:15.520
"Oh, they're being noisy over at the Fuushin Gazette again."

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:19.810
"They cause nothing but trouble!"

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:23.970
"Maybe we should just boycott them. What do you think?"

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:27.660
"That is a fine idea you just had there!"

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:31.970
"Oh stop it! Stop it!"

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:34.180
And if that

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:37.490
were ever to happen...!

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:40.410
Chief, please calm down!

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:44.020
At any rate, that's the deal,

00:08:44.020 --> 00:08:46.460
so don't scream like that again.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:49.310
Well, I'm going to bed.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:51.430
I'm very sorry!

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:55.800
Don't worry about her.

00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:59.140
The dark scared you, right?

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:00.080
It did.

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:05.290
Well, that's why the Chief lit all these candles.

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:08.110
I mean, she's even cheaper than I am,

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:11.160
so there's no other reason for her to light all these candles.

00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:15.300
She just can't be honest.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:17.850
Oh, hot! Hot! Hot!

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:30.960
Doesn't this warm light remind you of summer?

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:32.550
Yeah!

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:48.200
That reminds me of this one time

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:50.890
when Yuuki and I were small and

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:53.770
we got locked in the storehouse because we were causing mischief.

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:56.100
Wow, a storehouse?

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:58.560
Well, Yume's family is pretty rich.

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:02.750
And then Yuuki went and looked

00:10:02.750 --> 00:10:06.740
for a drawer with candles and matches.

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:16.140
Here you go, Yume.

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:19.260
Matches and candles!

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:25.010
So then you lit the candles and hid out there, huh?

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:27.280
You must have been so relieved!

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:29.170
Well, actually...

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:33.970
the storehouse caught fire and burned down.

00:10:33.970 --> 00:10:37.650
The goods that burnt up were worth hundreds of millions of yen...

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:44.380
You get scared so easily, Kana.

00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:49.040
I can't help it! If something's scary, it's scary.

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:52.480
This reminds me

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:56.880
of the time when I used to work as a corpse cleaner.

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:59.810
A-a corpse cleaner?!

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:04.270
Easy prey. Easy prey here.

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:06.650
What is it?

00:11:06.650 --> 00:11:09.860
Come on then, Haru-haru.  It's your turn.

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:13.890
Me? Well, let me think.

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:19.930
The truth is that I don't like all girls.

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:24.120
I only like girls between the ages of seven and fifteen!

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:27.030
Just kidding.

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:34.330
Did you know?

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:38.000
If you don't pay your utilities,

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:41.710
they'll shut off your electricity, your gas, and your water,

00:11:41.710 --> 00:11:43.380
one by one!

00:11:45.230 --> 00:11:47.310
Oh, that rings true.

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:50.310
What about you, Mika-chan?

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:51.260
Uhm...

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:55.560
You know, like having seen the ghost of a dead person,

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:58.210
or some kind of horror story from school.

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:03.760
I can't take it anymore!

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:08.780
Forgive us, Kana-chan!

00:12:08.780 --> 00:12:10.310
We just got carried away

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:12.370
because you're so cute when you're scared.

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:13.530
That's right!

00:12:13.530 --> 00:12:15.360
Sorry, Kana-chan!

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:17.090
I'm very sorry.

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:20.910
I...

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:26.390
Please, will somebody, anybody...

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:29.530
go to the bathroom with me?

00:12:29.530 --> 00:12:33.940
I can't hold it any longer!

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:46.450
A blue paper roll, a red paper roll, a yellow paper roll.

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:50.990
A blue paper roll, a red paper roll, a yellow paper roll!

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:53.630
Promise that you'll wait for me right there!

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:57.200
Are you still there? Say something, please!

00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:58.100
I'm so scared!

00:12:58.100 --> 00:13:01.530
Don't worry; we're right here!

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:03.390
I'm sure that's some kind of sin:

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:06.310
Making a tender young girl

00:13:06.310 --> 00:13:09.000
wait until she can't even hold it anymore!

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:10.850
I did hold it!

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:16.990
Eek! It looks like a human face!

00:13:19.170 --> 00:13:22.330
Eek! The ceiling is dripping!

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:25.510
I need to get out!

00:13:28.130 --> 00:13:32.730
No, there's no paper!

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:41.910
It's paper for you, paper!

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:45.710
I guess this means that God really knows everything you do.

00:13:45.710 --> 00:13:47.320
This is so half-baked.

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:52.970
I'm sorry I made all of you go with me.

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:56.710
We're all knights protecting you, Kana-chan...

00:13:56.710 --> 00:13:59.850
Escorting you to your chamber.

00:13:59.850 --> 00:14:03.860
We all have to go to our rooms anyway.

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:07.720
Oshikura cakes. Oshikura cakes!

00:14:07.720 --> 00:14:09.230
Then let's go.

00:14:22.180 --> 00:14:24.920
Something just touched me...

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:26.800
What, where?

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:29.600
Can you cut it out?

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:32.740
There's something here, too!

00:14:32.740 --> 00:14:34.610
How scary!

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:40.290
Yume-san, please stop that!

00:14:40.290 --> 00:14:48.060
My Yume touched someone else's skin... someone else's....

00:14:49.930 --> 00:14:51.330
The hunt is on.

00:14:55.100 --> 00:14:57.250
This is your room, Kana?

00:14:57.250 --> 00:14:59.230
It's an old room you know, so watch out!

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:01.790
Something may come out tonight!

00:15:03.650 --> 00:15:05.340
Geez, Yume.

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:07.300
I was just fooling around.

00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:12.140
Something just touched me again!

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:14.540
I haven't touched you yet!

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:15.730
Huh?

00:15:16.190 --> 00:15:21.710
I thought I'd hold your hand because you're scared.

00:15:21.710 --> 00:15:26.460
It wasn't my hand though. It brushed against my leg.

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:30.560
I want to brush up against you too, Kana-chan.

00:15:30.560 --> 00:15:32.340
Well, it wasn't me.

00:15:32.340 --> 00:15:35.170
Yume was touching me.

00:15:35.170 --> 00:15:38.690
That's right. Yuuki and I were together.

00:15:38.690 --> 00:15:40.710
Then that means that...

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:42.620
Maybe...

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:44.240
It's come out.

00:15:44.830 --> 00:15:47.630
Because this place is so old.

00:15:48.060 --> 00:15:54.380
Well, something's been by my legs for a while now.

00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:00.360
Calm down, calm down!

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:05.170
That's right, we need to stay calm.

00:16:05.170 --> 00:16:08.470
It's Hina-chan's fault, 'cause she said all those scary things!

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:12.640
There really was something there though!

00:16:12.640 --> 00:16:13.990
I'm scared!

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:16.680
Grandma, help!

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:19.810
Hey, stop pushing!

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:37.310
What's all this noise?

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:41.850
Chief!

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:43.240
Chief! It's here!

00:16:43.240 --> 00:16:45.200
Something came out in the dark, Chief, and it was brushing against our legs.

00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:46.680
We were all together, but it still tried to get us!

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:48.520
It's scary here at your place!

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:51.660
What are you guys blathering about?

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:54.940
All right, the light was out like this.

00:16:54.940 --> 00:16:57.330
We were all standing together.

00:16:57.330 --> 00:17:01.870
And then something came out and brushed up against our legs.

00:17:02.510 --> 00:17:05.970
It's back!

00:17:14.290 --> 00:17:16.290
So what brushed up against us...

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:17.670
Bunta, was that you?

00:17:17.670 --> 00:17:19.530
There are other cats here too.

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:25.650
They're all over!

00:17:29.970 --> 00:17:32.170
You were finally getting some rest,

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:34.530
but then all this ruckus happened, so...

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:37.960
You let all these cats in here?

00:17:37.960 --> 00:17:38.730
You got a problem with that?

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:40.110
Nope.

00:17:40.110 --> 00:17:41.190
Now I get it!

00:17:41.190 --> 00:17:46.190
You let the cats in so they could get out of the typhoon.

00:17:46.190 --> 00:17:47.530
That's right.

00:17:47.530 --> 00:17:50.240
Which is why I also asked you guys to keep it down.

00:17:53.880 --> 00:17:58.770
Oh good, they were just cats.

00:17:58.770 --> 00:18:00.590
What's so good about it?

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:04.870
Do you all have any idea what time it is right now?

00:18:04.870 --> 00:18:08.930
Not really... oh! It's already two in the morning!

00:18:08.930 --> 00:18:13.420
That's right. You have one hour before the morning delivery arrives,

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:19.230
so clean up all this stuff and the candles you used until then.

00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:21.700
All right, get it done.

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:23.460
Okay.

00:18:23.460 --> 00:18:26.180
Do we really have to pull an all-nighter?

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:27.880
Don't worry about it.

00:18:27.880 --> 00:18:30.450
It's Sunday, so it's not like we have school.

00:18:31.070 --> 00:18:34.630
We can sleep after we make the morning rounds.

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:36.400
That's right.

00:18:37.900 --> 00:18:43.740
I'm very sorry. I feel like this is all my fault.

00:18:45.150 --> 00:18:46.600
I'm very sorry!

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:48.040
It's not your fault at all.

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:50.560
If anyone's to blame, it's us.

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:54.530
It's all my fault!

00:18:54.850 --> 00:18:57.480
If the perp is so happy...

00:18:57.480 --> 00:18:59.830
...nobody can really be mad, huh?

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:03.210
This is what I was talking about.

00:19:03.210 --> 00:19:05.870
I guess getting along too well can be problematic as well.

00:19:07.220 --> 00:19:08.290
Yeah!

00:19:10.150 --> 00:19:13.940
It looks like the typhoon has passed.

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:15.550
Really?

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:19.830
Wow, what a beautiful sky!

00:19:20.330 --> 00:19:23.190
It looks like it's going to be another hot day.

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:26.860
Good morning, Chief.

00:19:26.860 --> 00:19:28.420
So, I have a question for you.

00:19:28.420 --> 00:19:29.060
Yes?

00:19:29.740 --> 00:19:34.170
It's five in the morning and the delivery truck hasn't arrived yet.

00:19:34.170 --> 00:19:35.800
What does that mean?

00:19:36.810 --> 00:19:38.610
We can't make the delivery.

00:19:38.610 --> 00:19:39.900
Nope.

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:41.800
The correct answer is:

00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:44.130
They couldn't make the delivery,

00:19:44.130 --> 00:19:47.020
and we're getting massive amounts of complaints.

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:51.940
And then...

00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:12.340
I'm done with my deliveries.

00:20:12.670 --> 00:20:14.410
Good morning, Kana.

00:20:14.410 --> 00:20:15.790
Good morning!

00:20:16.180 --> 00:20:17.740
Thank you.

00:20:17.740 --> 00:20:20.060
They've been waiting here for you for a while.

00:20:20.640 --> 00:20:23.000
What are you doing here?

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:25.120
Well...

00:20:25.120 --> 00:20:26.820
We wanted to apologize for yesterday.

00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:29.580
Oh, but it wasn't a big deal.

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:34.160
I couldn't ignore that you looked so lonely yesterday.

00:20:34.160 --> 00:20:35.940
Would you like to go

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:40.010
with us to deliver the cake to the teacher?

00:20:40.930 --> 00:20:42.860
I would, but

00:20:42.860 --> 00:20:46.970
I actually have to make everyone breakfast now.

00:20:46.970 --> 00:20:48.480
It's fine.

00:20:48.860 --> 00:20:50.490
Why don't you just go?

00:20:50.490 --> 00:20:52.360
Everyone's just going to go

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:54.730
straight to bed after the all-nighter.

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:57.680
Just set it up, and then you can go.

00:20:58.090 --> 00:21:00.090
Thank you, Chief!

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:04.310
Just one second, I'm going to change.

00:21:10.430 --> 00:21:17.800
Grandma, it looks like the weird feeling in my heart left with the typhoon.

00:21:17.800 --> 00:21:25.310
Everyone is so nice and it really makes me so happy.

00:21:46.290 --> 00:21:49.520
Bunta, are you thanking us for yesterday?

00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:52.710
You're such a good cat, Bunta.

00:21:52.710 --> 00:21:58.640
N-No, he isn't!!

00:23:29.930 --> 00:23:44.900
My First Welcome

00:23:30.910 --> 00:23:33.520
My First Welcome

00:23:33.520 --> 00:23:34.520
Egg nog.

00:23:34.520 --> 00:23:35.360
Giodone.

00:23:35.360 --> 00:23:36.470
N-Neo-greco.

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:37.550
Come at the Monet.

00:23:37.550 --> 00:23:38.770
NeNe's oboe.

00:23:38.770 --> 00:23:39.920
Ooh! Chardonnay.

00:23:39.920 --> 00:23:43.100
Ne again? But there aren't any more words that start with "ne"!

00:23:43.100 --> 00:23:44.890
He he he.
